        "tasks": [
          {
            "taskId": "s1",
            "status": "changes_requested",
            "summary": "Completed inspection of both submitted files, the pinned issue, acceptance requirements, and relevant test assertions. All four call sites use NODE_BIN, but runtime resolution has two path-handling defects and the tests do not guarantee a node-free PATH.",
            "findings": [
              {
                "severity": "MED",
                "location": "scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:61-64",
                "message": "Convert the selected runtime to an absolute path before pinning it.",
                "rationale": "An executable relative override such as ./tools/node passes validation and is returned unchanged. Likewise, command -v can return tools/node for a relative PATH entry. stop_managed_daemon can execute that path from the caller's directory, but spawn_daemon changes to DAEMON_ROOT before executing it, causing startup to fail or select a different executable. This violates the explicit absolute-path requirement. Add a regression with differing caller and daemon directories.",
                "evidenceReferences": [
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:scripts/daemon-ctl.sh",
                  "c249074026b8fad12105ce5fb9854935d6a72ae4:docs/standalone/daemon-ctl-sh-fails-node-command-E202611129d4523c7/ISSUE.md",
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts"
                ]
              },
              {
                "severity": "MED",
                "location": "scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:86",
                "message": "Preserve internal whitespace in the recorded runtime path.",
                "rationale": "The substitution removes every whitespace character, so a recorded executable such as /Applications/Node Tools/bin/node becomes /Applications/NodeTools/bin/node. When earlier resolution candidates are unavailable, a valid recorded runtime therefore produces exit 2. Read the path without deleting internal spaces and add a recorded-runtime regression using a directory containing spaces.",
                "evidenceReferences": [
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:scripts/daemon-ctl.sh",
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts"
                ]
              },
              {
                "severity": "MED",
                "location": "src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts:28",
                "message": "Construct a genuinely node-free test PATH instead of assuming system directories lack Node.",
                "rationale": "GUI_PATH includes /usr/bin and /bin, which can contain Node on supported Linux installations. There, the no-runtime test resolves the system Node and fails its exit-2 assertion; the recorded-runtime and well-known-location tests can execute system Node instead of exercising their intended branches. Build a controlled tools directory containing the required shell utilities but no node.",
                "evidenceReferences": [
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts"
                ]
              },
              {
                "severity": "LOW",
                "location": "src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts:191-203",
                "message": "Assert stopping the running fixture through daemon-ctl.sh.",
                "rationale": "The acceptance check requests node-free start and stop coverage. The stop test only handles an absent daemon, while the startup test ends with process.kill(SIGKILL). Neither asserts that the script stops a running daemon under the node-free environment. Extend the lifecycle test to invoke stop and assert process/socket cleanup.",
                "evidenceReferences": [
                  "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts",
                  "c249074026b8fad12105ce5fb9854935d6a72ae4:docs/standalone/daemon-ctl-sh-fails-node-command-E202611129d4523c7/ISSUE.md"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "testCoverage": {
              "assessment": "verified",
              "explanation": "Inspected every new test body and assertion, plus existing script-update, macOS routing, and Linux lifecycle coverage. The seven new cases assert explicit override resolution, recorded fallback, PATH preference, missing-runtime exit, absent-daemon stop, invalid override, and startup/status through a location override. Missing relative-path, whitespace-path, and running-daemon stop assertions are identified above. Existing Linux lifecycle assertions cover running stop with an ordinary inherited PATH; macOS routing uses a Node shim and does not establish node-free supervised lifecycle behavior. Naming follows local shell conventions such as DAEMON_ROOT, STOP_WAIT_SECS, spawn_daemon and socket_status; no material separation-of-concerns or wire-compatibility issue was found.",
              "evidenceReferences": [
                "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-node-path.test.ts",
                "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/daemon-ctl-source.test.ts",
                "a6ab1afcdb71659e977c98effa859f4e604662fe:src/daemon/__tests__/macos-upgrade-routing.test.ts",
